        "doc": "Extended summer load‑shedding has serious repercussions beyond inconvenience. Students study with phone flashlights, small retailers lose perishable inventory, and tradespeople lose unpaid productive hours that cannot be made up. Those who can afford solar panels or UPS batteries manage better, exacerbating inequality. Economists contend that dependable electricity is essential for education and income, not a luxury."
